    "q-140322": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140322",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Rewrite $-({x}^{2}-12x+35)$ by completing the square.",
      "worked_solution": "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-12x+35\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+35\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${6}^{2},$ writing the constant term $35$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}}_{⏟}-{6}^{2}+35\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-6)^{2}-{6}^{2}+35\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-6)^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}-12x+35) & =-({(x-6)}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =-{(x-6)}^{2}+1 \\\\  & =1-(x-6)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
